### Expected

When a `--parallel` worker dies unexpectedly, the synthetic `"Uncaught error outside test suite"` failure should have a `.file` property pointing to the spec that crashed — same as any other test failure.

### Actual

The synthetic failure has `file: undefined`. Every reporter (JSON, xUnit, spec, custom) and any tooling that keys on `test.file` loses track of which spec crashed.

Confirmed on **11.7.5** and **12.0.0**.

### Minimal, Complete and Verifiable Example

```js
// crash.js
describe('crash', () => {
  it('passes before death', () => {});
  after(() => process.exit(1));
});
```

```js
// healthy.js
describe('healthy', () => { it('ok', () => {}); });
```

```bash
npx mocha --parallel --jobs 2 --reporter json crash.js healthy.js
```

Output (trimmed):

```json
{
  "failures": [{
    "title": "Uncaught error outside test suite",
    "file": null
  }]
}

```

All worker-death paths (`process.exit`, OOM kill, segfault, unhandled rejection) flow through the same `pool.run` rejection → `_uncaught` path, so a fix covers them uniformly.

### Versions

- `mocha --version`: 11.7.5 (also reproduced on 12.0.0)
- `node --version`: v22.22.2
- OS: macOS Darwin 25.6.0

### Additional Info

**Root cause:** The catch in `_createFileRunner` (`parallel-buffered-runner.cjs` ~225) re-throws without `err.file = file`. `Runner#_uncaught` (`runner.cjs` ~1142) then creates a phony Runnable without propagating it.

**Proposed fix** — two changes, 6 lines, no API changes (`file` is already a standard Runnable property):

1\. `lib/nodejs/parallel-buffered-runner.cjs` — tag the error before re-throwing:

```diff
           if (this.allowUncaught) {
             this._state = ABORTING;
             await pool.terminate(true);
           }
+          if (err && typeof err === 'object') {
+            try { err.file = file; } catch { /* frozen or non-writable */ }
+          }
           throw err;
```

2\. `lib/runner.cjs` — propagate to the phony Runnable:

```diff
     runnable = new Runnable("Uncaught error outside test suite");
     debug("uncaught(): no current Runnable; created a phony one");
     runnable.parent = this.suite;
+    if (err.file) {
+      runnable.file = err.file;
+    }
```

**Related:**
- #3200 — broader request for file in failure reports (open since 2017, `semver-major`). This fix is narrower: parallel worker deaths only, mechanical propagation of a value already in scope, no API surface change.
- #6233 — complementary: fixes whether/how a worker failure is reported (exit code, `STATE_RUNNING`), but does not touch file attribution.

> @mark-wiemer Thanks for your reply. "Copying the docs works" is because you have `.timeout(1000)` on `it()`, delete that and you'll find out the issue. I give you this snippet for example, by default mocha timesout 2000, so case failing for timeout has to be longer than that.
> 
> ```javascript
> describe('my suite', () => {
>   it('my test', async () => {
>     await new Promise((resolve) => {
>       setTimeout(resolve, 4000);
>     });
>   });
> }).timeout(5000);
> ```
> The issue is because mocha runs the "hook function" immediately, in which the test cases get created with a default timeout 2000. After that `suite.timeout(5000)` changes `suite._timeout` but has no effect on cases inside it.
> I'd open a new issue if you consider it a bug and would fix it. 

